instruction:
Bug: `JEPATrainer` in `luthi/v2/jepa_runner.py` is supposed to keep the newest `checkpoint.rolling_slots` checkpoints (`ckpt_*.pt` under the run's `checkpoints/` folder), so that `resume_from_latest` can fall back to an older slot when the newest file is corrupt. In practice only one checkpoint ever survives on disk. With 3 slots, writing a second checkpoint deletes the first.

Fix the rolling cap in `JEPATrainer._checkpoint` so that:
- writing fewer checkpoints than `rolling_slots` deletes nothing;
- the directory fills up to the cap;
- once over the cap, exactly the newest `rolling_slots` files remain.

After the fix, a corrupt newest checkpoint should make `resume_from_latest` load the next-older slot.
